Tool #3: finalize
I finalized the dataset. The code tested the incumbent, the 4-member ensemble m-eurosat-L2-006, on the test split. I only see the vault hash: sha256:dfae022ff91b569528b29f55e3abafde495488890260aa8a0690c8fb283f8581.

The ensemble scored 98.90% on validation. That ties the best single model, m-eurosat-0010, so I kept the ensemble as the more robust choice. The differences between the top candidates (98.70–98.90%) are within seed noise. The ensemble averages two ResNet18 runs (0010, 0008), one ResNet50 run (0009) and an extra ResNet18 seed (0015), all with SSL4EO MoCo weights.

About 4.2 minutes of the Level 1 pot and 8.7 minutes of the Level 2 pot went unused.[finalize] end: 3 tool calls, 0.2 min, tokens {'inputTokens': 5905, 'outputTokens': 483, 'totalTokens': 10351} (transcript m-eurosat__main__chain.finalize.md)
